# G2 floors (plans/DROP_LIBURING.md Phase 6): the epoll fallback's throughput
# as a fraction of the io_uring backend's, per benchmark. Initial values are
# deliberately conservative and were set before measurement; the ratchet only
# tightens — record the merged numbers here and never lower one.
# The keys are the bench's metric names (scripts/bench/io_bench.yo:
# pingpong, parked, timer, file). Until 2026-09-27 the echo floor was keyed
# echo_min_ratio after the bench had renamed its metric, so it checked
# nothing (issues/fixed/linux-io-runtime-minor-defects-from-the-drop-liburing-audit.md).
pingpong_min_ratio=1.00
parked_min_ratio=0.50
timer_min_ratio=0.90
# file ops: no floor by design — the epoll fallback completes them
# synchronously (macOS parity, plans/DROP_LIBURING.md Phase 5); the number is
# recorded for information.

# Stock-Linux baseline (GitHub ubuntu-latest x86_64, the io-budgets job,
# 2026-09-27): epoll/uring ops-per-second ratios, microsecond timings.
#
#   run                         pingpong  parked  timer  file
#   36334993270 (two-enter poll)   1.739   0.754  0.963  1.309
#   36337258876 (one-enter poll)   1.361   0.652  0.967  1.172
#
# The second row is the current code; the ring got faster (pingpong 562K ->
# 680K ops/s, parked 534K -> 614K), so the ratios fell. Floors sit about 25%
# under it for runner noise: pingpong 1.00, parked 0.50, timer stays 0.90
# (already under 0.967). Both backends now make one syscall per inline op; epoll
# still wins the inline ping-pong because a plain recv/send is cheaper than an
# io_uring_enter, and loses the parked one (recv EAGAIN + epoll_ctl +
# epoll_wait + recv + epoll_ctl against one SQE).
#
# Earlier baseline (WSL2 6.6, i7, nix clang -O2, 2026-09-26, the Phase 6
# merge): epoll/uring ratios — echo 1.75, timer 20.3, file 7.1. The epoll
# fallback completes this suite's inline patterns without kernel round-trips,
# so it is FASTER than the ring on this box; WSL2's io_uring is also known to
# carry extra per-op cost, and that bench's timings were whole milliseconds
# and its timer ran the punted timerfd READ. Superseded by the table above.
#
# G1 (zero ring-path regression), same box: echo identical (142857 ops/ms
# units on both the Phase-1 and Phase-6 binaries); timer/file within run
# variance (+8%/+16% on 300 ms runs).
